WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.336
The children walked in a slow parade toward the castle.

2
00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:13.559
They were sure that they had stepped into a fairy tale.

3
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:19.184
At last they arrived in a large hall filled with wooden benches and tables.

4
00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:24.456
Suits of armor and old flags stood against the walls.

5
00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.387
"Wait here," said the princess.

6
00:00:27.388 --> 00:00:29.418
"And don't talk while I'm gone.

7
00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:31.594
This castle is full of magic.

8
00:00:31.595 --> 00:00:34.659
I don't know what will happen if you talk."

9
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.443
Jimmy wanted to say that he didn't think anything would happen.

10
00:00:38.444 --> 00:00:40.860
But he didn't.

11
00:00:40.861 --> 00:00:44.069
The princess returned, carrying a tray.

12
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.980
"I could only find bread and cheese and water, but it doesn't matter.

13
00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:53.405
They'll turn into anything you like—unless you have some dreadful secret fault.

14
00:00:53.406 --> 00:00:56.768
What would you like to eat?"

15
00:00:56.769 --> 00:01:00.433
"Roast chicken," said Kathleen.

16
00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:04.876
She watched as the princess cut some bread and laid it on a plate.

17
00:01:04.877 --> 00:01:10.383
"Green peas?" The princess cut a piece of cheese and laid it beside the bread.

18
00:01:10.384 --> 00:01:13.293
Then she handed the plate to Kathleen.

19
00:01:13.294 --> 00:01:16.829
The boys asked for roast beef and cabbage.

20
00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:20.756
Kathleen cut the bread as if she was eating roast chicken.

21
00:01:20.757 --> 00:01:24.383
But it still looked and tasted like bread.

22
00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:29.380
She wondered what her secret fault was as she watched the boys eat their food.

23
00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:32.554
"This is a game, isn't it?" said Jimmy.

24
00:01:32.555 --> 00:01:36.647
"Pretending we're eating roast beef."

25
00:01:36.648 --> 00:01:39.306
"But it is beef. Look at it."

26
00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:42.548
The princess opened her eyes very wide.

27
00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:49.017
"Of course," said Jimmy weakly. "I was just joking."

28
00:01:49.018 --> 00:01:51.478
Everyone was very hungry.

29
00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:55.093
They ate and drank and felt much better.

30
00:01:55.094 --> 00:02:02.777
"Now if you're finished," said the princess, "I'll show you my treasures."

31
00:02:02.778 --> 00:02:08.264
They followed her down a long hall to some steps.

32
00:02:08.265 --> 00:02:14.508
Underneath the steps was a door hidden by a tapestry.

33
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:21.086
"This door leads to my private apartments," said the princess.

34
00:02:21.087 --> 00:02:26.007
She guided them through a dark corridor until they came to a room.

35
00:02:26.008 --> 00:02:30.016
The princess went in first and threw open the shutters.

36
00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:33.464
The small domed room was filled with light.

37
00:02:33.465 --> 00:02:36.907
Its blue ceiling was painted with gold stars.

38
00:02:36.908 --> 00:02:39.091
But the room was empty.

39
00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:43.569
"Where are the treasures?" Kathleen asked politely.

40
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:47.047
"Don't you see them?" said the princess.

41
00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:49.953
"No," said Jimmy.

42
00:02:49.954 --> 00:02:52.094
"And don't try fooling us again.

43
00:02:52.095 --> 00:02:54.382
There's nothing here."

44
00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:58.609
"Then I guess I'll have to say the charm," said the princess.

45
00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.348
"Close your eyes, please."

46
00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:04.700
The princess chanted some nonsense words.

47
00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:07.923
There was a creaking, rustling sound.

48
00:03:07.924 --> 00:03:10.896
"Open your eyes now."

49
00:03:10.897 --> 00:03:13.906
The children could not believe their eyes.

50
00:03:13.907 --> 00:03:19.874
Silver dishes, gold cups, and diamond crowns lined shelves around the room.

51
00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:24.132
All around were piles of necklaces, rings, and bracelets.

52
00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:27.337
"Oh my!" Gerald whispered.

53
00:03:27.338 --> 00:03:32.259
"Now do you believe I can do magic?" asked the princess.

54
00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.517
"Yes!" said Kathleen. "May we touch?"

55
00:03:36.518 --> 00:03:38.476
"Go ahead."

56
00:03:38.477 --> 00:03:42.291
The children had great fun playing with the treasures.

57
00:03:42.292 --> 00:03:44.945
Suddenly Kathleen had a thought.

58
00:03:44.946 --> 00:03:47.473
"Do your parents know you're awake?"

59
00:03:47.474 --> 00:03:52.789
"Oh . . . uh . . . yes," said the princess.

60
00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.281
"I told them when I got the bread and cheese.

61
00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:56.531
They're busy right now.

62
00:03:56.532 --> 00:03:59.551
Here, try this bracelet."

63
00:03:59.552 --> 00:04:03.236
"What's this old stuff over here?" asked Jimmy.

64
00:04:03.237 --> 00:04:07.345
"Those are all magic things!" said the princess.

65
00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:11.126
"What does this ring do?" asked Gerald.

66
00:04:11.127 --> 00:04:13.136
"It makes you invisible."

67
00:04:13.137 --> 00:04:17.677
"I'd like to try that," said Jimmy.

68
00:04:17.678 --> 00:04:21.335
"No, I'm the only one who can touch these things.

69
00:04:21.336 --> 00:04:24.673
If anyone else tries, they'll lose their magic.

70
00:04:24.674 --> 00:04:27.366
Close your eyes and I'll demonstrate the ring."

71
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.748
The children closed their eyes.

72
00:04:29.749 --> 00:04:32.852
"Now count to fifty."

73
00:04:32.853 --> 00:04:34.967
Gerald counted aloud.

74
00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:41.693
Everyone could hear a creaking, rustling sound. ". . . 49, 50."

75
00:04:41.694 --> 00:04:44.075
The children opened their eyes.

76
00:04:44.076 --> 00:04:51.149
The jewels had vanished, and so had the princess.

